# Task 05: Supervised Learning - Classification

## Objective
The objective of this task is to build and evaluate classification models for predicting employee attrition using machine learning techniques.

## Dataset
Dataset Used: IBM HR Analytics Employee Attrition & Performance

File Name:
WA_Fn-UseC_-HR-Employee-Attrition.csv

Target Variable:
Attrition

## Tools and Libraries
- Python
- Google Colab
- Pandas
- NumPy
- Matplotlib
- Seaborn
- Scikit-learn

## Steps Performed

### 1. Data Loading
- Loaded the dataset into a Pandas DataFrame.

### 2. Data Preprocessing
- Checked dataset structure.
- Encoded categorical variables using Label Encoding.
- Selected features and target variable.

### 3. Train-Test Split
- Split the dataset into 80% training data and 20% testing data.

### 4. Model Training
The following classification models were trained:
- Logistic Regression
- Decision Tree Classifier
- Random Forest Classifier

### 5. Model Evaluation
Evaluated each model using:
- Accuracy Score
- Confusion Matrix
- Classification Report

### 6. Visualization
- Generated a Confusion Matrix Heatmap for the best-performing model.

## Results

| Model | Accuracy |
|---------|---------|
| Logistic Regression | 0.860544 |
| Decision Tree | 0.765306 |
| Random Forest | 0.867347 |

## Best Model
Random Forest achieved the highest accuracy and provided the most reliable predictions on the test dataset.

## Files Included
- Task5_Classification.ipynb
- confusion_matrix.png
- README.md

## Conclusion
Three classification algorithms were implemented and compared. Random Forest performed the best among all models, making it the most suitable model for predicting employee attrition in this dataset.
